@c.sprite:C{al=binary;ch=[@i.px,@i.pl,@i.vw,@i.sa,@i.al,@i.li];li=~192:Flat unlit fill with no interior ramp or dithering. Form is described by the dark #25354A outline alone, because reference.png contains no fourth colour and therefore supplies no shading ramp.;nm=~46:Teal scout robot 32x32 side-view sample sprite;pl=[~7:#25354A,~7:#56B5BC,~7:#F4DDA2];px=[32,32];sa=nearest;vw=side}
@f.sprite:F{ct=@c.sprite;kd=sprite;nm=~50:Teal scout robot representative sprite PNG (32x32);rq=[@q.canvas,@q.palette,@q.alpha,@q.nearest,@q.identity,@q.webdisplay];tk=@t.sample}
@i.al:I{ky=~2:al;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief,@s.refobs];st=confirmed;vl=binary;wh=@user;wy=~146:The owner requires binary transparency. reference.png already measures 0 fractional-alpha pixels, so the reference is consistent with this policy.}
@i.delivery_target:I{ky=~15:delivery_target;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief];st=confirmed;vl=~99:A single PNG file displayed in a web prototype at an integer scale with nearest-neighbour sampling.;wh=@user;wy=~119:Stated delivery destination. It sets the integer-presentation requirement and the engine-domain criterion q.webdisplay.}
@i.eye_presentation:I{ky=~16:eye_presentation;pr=@project;so=[];st=proposed;vl=~67:Both eyes remain visible on the facing plane of a side-facing body.;wh=@actor;wy=~418:Not stated by the owner, and the brief's two requirements pull apart: a strict profile head shows one eye, but the owner requires two eyes and the reference shows two. Proposed resolution is the common 2D convention of a side-facing body with a frontally-read face. This is the main artistic risk the representative sample must settle before any family expansion; a returned profile head with one eye fails q.identity.}
@i.family_scope:I{ky=~12:family_scope;pr=@project;so=[];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~219:The owner defers family expansion until this sample is reviewed and has not named the members (poses, directions, states or variants). Required before the family and delivery operation can record members and a baseline.}
@i.features:I{ky=~8:features;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief,@s.refobs];st=confirmed;vl={antennae=2;body_color=~7:#56B5BC;eye_color=~7:#F4DDA2;eyes=2;subject=~11:scout robot};wh=@user;wy=~207:Feature inventory required by the owner and corroborated by the reference: two antennae rising from the top of the head in the outline colour, and two pale-yellow eyes as separate clusters on the upper body.}
@i.ground_shadow:I{ky=~13:ground_shadow;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief,@s.refobs];st=confirmed;vl=~143:No ground shadow, contact shadow or ground-contact cluster is drawn into the sprite; the silhouette must remain one connected opaque component.;wh=@user;wy=~143:The owner requires no ground shadow. reference.png measures exactly 1 opaque connected component, confirming the reference carries none either.}
@i.li:I{ky=~2:li;pr=@project;so=[];st=proposed;vl=~192:Flat unlit fill with no interior ramp or dithering. Form is described by the dark #25354A outline alone, because reference.png contains no fourth colour and therefore supplies no shading ramp.;wh=@actor;wy=~315:Not stated by the owner. Proposed because a three-colour palette leaves no value ramp, and reference.png shows a completely flat teal fill with zero interior shading. Adopting any shading would require a fourth colour and would break the confirmed palette. The sample exists to test this proposal, not to assume it.}
@i.outline:I{ky=~7:outline;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief,@s.refobs];st=confirmed;vl=~7:#25354A;wh=@user;wy=~183:The owner requires dark outlines. The only dark colour in the reference palette is #25354A, used in the reference as a uniform two-pixel border enclosing the body and as the antennae.}
@i.pl:I{ky=~2:pl;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief,@s.refobs,@s.refpng];st=confirmed;vl=[~7:#25354A,~7:#56B5BC,~7:#F4DDA2];wh=@user;wy=~245:The owner requires 'the reference palette'. A colour census of reference.png returns exactly three opaque colours: #25354A outline/antennae (180 px), #56B5BC body (186 px), #F4DDA2 eyes (24 px). No fourth colour exists, so this list is complete.}
@i.provider:I{ky=~8:provider;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief,@s.discovery,@s.caps];st=observed;vl=~128:PixelLab is the owner's named generator, but no PixelLab tool is callable in this session and no PixelLab credential is present.;wh=@actor;wy=~389:The owner named PixelLab. Discovery of the actual session tool surface found only the local pixl-local MCP server, whose own instructions state PixelLab must be connected separately. pixl_capabilities is a dated documentation inventory that reports live_discovery false, so it cannot supply the observed schema that job-prepare requires. This blocks generation, not planning or evaluation.}
@i.px:I{ky=~2:px;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief,@s.refpng];st=confirmed;vl=[32,32];wh=@user;wy=~116:The owner states 32 by 32; reference.png measures exactly 32x32 with the art inset from every edge (bbox 7,3-25,28).}
@i.sa:I{ky=~2:sa;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief];st=confirmed;vl=nearest;wh=@user;wy=~82:The owner will display the PNG with nearest-neighbour sampling in a web prototype.}
@i.vw:I{ky=~2:vw;pr=@project;so=[@s.brief];st=confirmed;vl=side;wh=@user;wy=~161:The owner states side view. reference.png does not itself demonstrate a view; it is bilaterally symmetric and supplies palette, features and edge treatment only.}
@i.web_prototype:I{ky=~13:web_prototype;pr=@project;so=[];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~223:The owner has not identified the web prototype's repository, framework, page or asset path. Until it is named, the engine-domain criterion q.webdisplay cannot be executed and must be recorded unavailable rather than passed.}
@k.alpha:K{ap=[transparent_sprites_75353d50,glows_19e4066b,sprite_atlases_07b42f1f];ck=[~75:Binary-alpha assets contain only 0 and 255 unless an exception is declared.,~56:Composited fixtures agree with the declared alpha model.];nm=~38:Declare alpha and compositing behavior;op=[~55:Keep alpha policy separate from RGB palette membership.,~84:Use the chosen compositing equation consistently through export, import and display.,~73:Inspect edges against light and dark backgrounds after round-trip import.];rk=[~78:Fully transparent RGB channels can differ without changing visible appearance.];rq=[~78:RGBA interpretation, straight or premultiplied alpha, and allowed alpha levels];so=[@s.kb.alpha];tg=[~14:alpha-contract]}
@k.integer:K{ap=[strict_grid_games_a7cd2a47,pixel_previews_014b1177,sprite_delivery_638f99a7];ck=[~75:A logical pixel expands into a uniform scale-by-scale block in the fixture.,~66:No new colours appear during opaque nearest-neighbour enlargement.];nm=~59:Render at a declared logical grid and inspect device pixels;op=[~87:Render or sample at the logical grid, then use a declared integer scale where required.,~83:Apply nearest sampling to image scaling and account for browser device pixel ratio.,~68:Inspect the final output, not only a CSS property or import setting.];rk=[~90:Noninteger scaling, arbitrary rotation and browser zoom can change displayed pixel widths.];rq=[~68:Logical resolution, camera convention and target viewport dimensions];so=[@s.kb.integer];tg=[~20:integer-presentation]}
@k.palette:K{ap=[indexed_sprites_40eaa310,limited_palette_styles_c8701d42,material_ramps_1ca01010];ck=[~45:Every checked pixel maps to an allowed index.,~64:Palette changes retain stable semantic meaning and transparency.];nm=~37:Declare and validate a scoped palette;op=[~75:Assign stable palette indices and reserve any transparent entry explicitly.,~96:Validate opaque pixels against the palette; keep lighting-output exemptions separately declared.,~86:Apply colour replacements by semantic ramp rather than unrestricted RGB interpolation.];rk=[~89:A fixed small palette is optional art direction, not a universal definition of pixel art.,~74:RGBA data can be palette-constrained without using an indexed file format.];rq=[~69:An approved RGBA palette, colour-space choice and transparency policy];so=[@s.kb.palette,@s.kb.palette.assets];tg=[~16:palette-contract]}
@k.silhouette:K{ap=[characters_25d939ff,inventory_icons_f7812ea4,interactive_props_25a44283];ck=[~59:Named identity landmarks remain visible at the target size.,~79:Required gaps stay open and interactive forms separate from their surroundings.];nm=~57:Evaluate identity using silhouette and target backgrounds;op=[~43:Render a flat opaque mask before detailing.,~91:Inspect major proportions, negative spaces and landmark separation at native logical scale.,~78:Compare the coloured asset on representative light, dark and busy backgrounds.];rk=[~66:Silhouette alone cannot validate faces, materials or fine symbols.,~62:No contrast ratio or component count proves aesthetic quality.];rq=[~73:Intended viewing scale, representative backgrounds and identity landmarks];so=[@s.kb.silhouette];tg=[~22:silhouette-readability]}
@project:P{br=~394:Produce a representative 32x32 side-view teal scout robot sprite with PixelLab, matching reference.png: two antennae, two yellow eyes, dark outlines, binary transparency, no ground shadow, and the reference palette. Deliver a PNG for nearest-neighbor display in a web prototype. Verify dimensions and palette mechanically and compare visually against the reference before expanding to a family.;ct=@c.sprite;in=[@i.px,@i.pl,@i.vw,@i.al,@i.sa,@i.li,@i.outline,@i.ground_shadow,@i.features,@i.eye_presentation,@i.delivery_target,@i.web_prototype,@i.provider,@i.family_scope];nm=~23:Teal Scout Robot Sample;ow=@user;sc=[@s.brief,@s.refobs,@s.refpng,@s.discovery,@s.caps]}
@q.alpha:Q{ck=~129:asset-check with alpha binary reports fractional_alpha_pixels 0 and no alpha failure, so every pixel's alpha is exactly 0 or 255.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~22:Transparency is binary;so=[@s.brief,@s.kb.alpha];wh=@actor}
@q.canvas:Q{ck=~109:asset-check on the delivered PNG reports frame_count 1 with width 32 and height 32, and no dimension failure.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~23:Canvas is exactly 32x32;so=[@s.brief];wh=@actor}
@q.identity:Q{ck=~426:Viewed by the agent at native 32x32 and at integer zoom, side by side with reference.png in one contact sheet: the sprite reads as a side-facing teal scout robot; exactly two antennae are visible above the head; exactly two yellow eyes are visible; a dark #25354A outline encloses the silhouette; the teal body fill is flat; and no shadow cluster, ground contact smear or stray detached pixel appears below or around the body.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~40:Reads as the referenced teal scout robot;so=[@s.brief,@s.refobs,@s.kb.silhouette];wh=@actor}
@q.nearest:Q{ck=~202:An 8x nearest-neighbour enlargement of the delivered PNG contains exactly the same set of visible colours as the 32x32 source, and every logical pixel maps to a uniform 8x8 block of a single RGBA value.;dm=other;md=local;nm=~46:Integer nearest-neighbour enlargement is clean;so=[@s.kb.integer];wh=@actor}
@q.palette:Q{ck=~172:asset-check with palette #25354A #56B5BC #F4DDA2 reports outside_palette_count 0 and visible_colors no greater than 3; every listed colour that appears is one of the three.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~39:Only the three reference colours appear;so=[@s.brief,@s.refobs];wh=@actor}
@q.webdisplay:Q{ck=~330:Loaded in the owner's actual web prototype at an integer scale with nearest sampling (for example image-rendering: pixelated), the sprite shows hard unblended pixel edges, introduces no colours outside the three-colour palette, and its transparent edges composite cleanly with no halo over both a light and a dark page background.;dm=engine;md=live;nm=~47:Displays correctly in the owner's web prototype;so=[@s.brief];wh=@actor}
